# Tests inherit the root configuration and drop one check.
#
# CHECK() records a failure and returns, so the analysis is not wrong about
# `CHECK(value.has_value()); use(*value);` -- the deref really does run when
# the check fails. It is dropped because the reading cost across every such
# pair outweighs it, and because a test that must not continue past a failed
# condition has REQUIRE() to say so.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access
